{"ts":"2026-07-24T20:08:24.767Z","author":"claude-code-agent","op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/6","value":{"created_at":"2026-07-24T20:08:24.767Z","author":"claude-code-agent","text":"Evidence: unchanged pnpm benchmark:scale:check passed three consecutive runs under supported Node v22.21.1. cli.create min was 275ms, 286ms, and 287ms (budget 310ms); create peak RSS was 102768640, 104648704, and 102649856 bytes (budget 115184640); claim peak RSS was 102375424, 103870464, and 104419328 bytes (budget 118031360). SDK create remained 5-7ms. Budgets, iteration count, transports, and feature coverage were unchanged. Root cause was startup parse cost compounded by default full-corpus similarity work; fixed via opt-in default governance, dependency-light scoring, selective create registration, cached settings reuse, and production bundle minification with source maps."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-24T20:08:24.767Z"}],"before_hash":"279b21ba2f3248caf64c2fce663c1f791f4a15f794584018ae398a515784d341","after_hash":"50d23901ae014f56418a362c6cfffb96392e0529bfc0b43d8b4c5f8b5b5839c8"}
